# Build context is the repo root (so deploy/ and server/ are both reachable).
# Everything below is either private, host-specific, or irrelevant at runtime.

# ---- The owner's real data. This MUST stay first and exhaustive. ----
# Anything in the build context can be COPYed into a layer, and layers are
# trivially extractable even if a later stage deletes the file. Recordings,
# transcripts, speaker embeddings and the command-signing key reach the
# container through a mounted volume at runtime, never through the image.
server/data/
**/*.opusraw
**/*.peaks
**/server_token
**/hermes.token
**/server_ed25519.key
**/config.toml

# ---- Not part of the server image ----
# The firmware and Android toolchains do not run on the server box (spec §9),
# and they are by far the largest directories in the repo.
firmware/
android/

# ---- Local environments and caches ----
# .venv holds macOS/arm64 wheels including MLX — wrong architecture, wrong OS.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.git/
.superpowers/

# ---- Not needed at runtime ----
# Tests carry audio fixtures; docs/ is gitignored design work.
server/tests/
docs/
*.md
